{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196803-spirits-of-cities","id":1196803,"title":"Spirits of cities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-18T08:26:30-07:00","id":1196803,"title":"Spirits of cities","content":"I have gotten the impression that you can very well have spirits that are spirits of entire cities. I seem to recall the newest iteration of Werewolf: the Forsaken having two spirits of Washington DC as rivals for that city.<br /> <br /> This is an idea that intrigues me and I have to wonder what type of rank would be appropriate for such a powerful being. Rank 3 for villages and small towns, 4 for smaller cities like Newcastle, Lille, Murmansk or Bergen, rank 5 for big cities like London, Paris, Moscow or Oslo?<br /> <br /> Could such spirits have Influence: Stockholm or Influence: London for example? Or would you have them have some other smaller influences that would be appropriate for its rank and niche?<br /> <br /> \u200bIn my games I imagine such spirits being more or less mobster kings, jealously guarding their city against those who would disturb it, ruthlessly hunting down contenders to its rule and cruelly cowing many lesser spirits into a feudal vassalage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T09:21:53-07:00","id":1196825,"title":"","content":"Alright can you describe them in more detail","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T10:31:38-07:00","id":1196848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196803-spirits-of-cities#post1196803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have gotten the impression that you can very well have spirits that are spirits of entire cities. I seem to recall the newest iteration of Werewolf: the Forsaken having two spirits of Washington DC as rivals for that city.</div> </div> </div> </div>City spirits are a thing. I believe that specific example is from DaveB's Mage game, Broken Diamond.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is an idea that intrigues me and I have to wonder what type of rank would be appropriate for such a powerful being. Rank 3 for villages and small towns, 4 for smaller cities like Newcastle, Lille, Murmansk or Bergen, rank 5 for big cities like London, Paris, Moscow or Oslo? </div> </div> </div>I think you'd go up a rank. London, Paris and Moscow and Oslo seem like they would have Rank 6. They're old and storied cities. Rank 3 seems very low, even for a village. But an alternative is to have the city spirit fractured or not fully realized. So like a Rank 5 spirit of west Murmansk with the river and port and a Rank 4 spirit of east Murmansk depicting more traditional city spirit elements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could such spirits have Influence: Stockholm or Influence: London for example? Or would you have them have some other smaller influences that would be appropriate for its rank and niche? </div> </div> </div>At a certain point I'd give them Influence: Cities (we've seen this Influence before in books) but I think some would depend on the city. West Murmansk would have river and trade Influences, for instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bIn my games I imagine such spirits being more or less mobster kings, jealously guarding their city against those who would disturb it, ruthlessly hunting down contenders to its rule and cruelly cowing many lesser spirits into a feudal vassalage. </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I'd expect when they were Rank 6 they wouldn't really need to, as they could just have vassals do that but that's basically how spirits are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T11:08:15-07:00","id":1196860,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the published (1E) intro module, &quot;Manitou Springs&quot; has the spirit of a tiny tourist trap at Rank 2 - although its town has been assaulted by a claimed for years. Its recommended as the pack's totem. I believe its main influence was over the town itself, with a dot in water. But this is one example. <br /> <br /> <br /> For my werewolf game a while ago, I've done a lot of consideration as to how spirits rise and fall in rank, and what those court politics are like. *Its not cannon*, but we don't have a lot of published descriptions to go off of.<br /> So if it helps, here's how I think of it:<br /> Spirits start out as reflections of a discrete thing; they grow in rank as that thing gains prominance and they branch out to general categories and multiple influences (by consuming more essence - implying intensive competition, even the consumption of their rivals).<br /> So a city spirit is never made whole cloth. It has an origin- often a landmark, industry, or event thats core to that city's identity. It was the river that was first settled as a trade port; the mine that fueled a manufacturing city; the annual festival that's unique to the town - at first bringing villagers together, then drawing tourists.<br /> It started off as this little discrete spirit, and it clawed its way up the local hierarchy, comsuming rival spirits of other important streets and events, beating the neighborhood spirits into paying tribute. Eventually, it became the dominant spirit - the most powerful and broadly encompassing out of the entire choir of city spirits. But, like all spirits, its original purpose and nature is fundamental to its identity. Its the city spirit and the spirit of the strawberry festival which has become iconic for the town.<br /> As cities grow and change, new spirits are born and try to oust the ruler, stealing vassals and building their own prominence. Sometimes they supplant the former ruler, sometimes their rise divides the city in half (or more), sometimes they become powerful but fold into subservience of the reigning city spirit - becoming iconic districts or subcultures secondary to the city's main character.<br /> <br /> So I strongly agree with the mobster comparison, from rise to reign to rivalry. I would also say that it's important to note what the spirit started as and what its rivals / vassals reflect to really get into the characterization of the city and its spirit politics. Maybe this isn't necessary for many games, but the Shadow is, in large part, living history.<br /> <br /> <br /> To judge its rank, my rule if thumb is 'one higher than its strongest rival' and using the various chart descriptions of each rank. I believe the spirits of whole nations / globally recognized landmarks were recommended as rank 6, while spirits of an entire species / werewolf tribal totems were rank 7. <br /> I could easily see a national capital or major global cities as being Rank 6 in those guidelines. Major regional hubs might be 5, and getting swiftly lower as the city gets smaller.<br /> If a small town's city spirit just has to beat out a few iconic streets / industries, it may be only Rank 2. But since NYC has globally recognized landmarks like Broadway, which are rank 4 or 5 themselves, it would likely be 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 03-18-2018, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T11:25:50-07:00","id":1196865,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: City Spirits</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12969-seraph\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12969\" data-vbnamecard=\"12969\">Seraph</a> Kitty eloquently covered the points I was going to make. Thinking of The City Spirit as the largest and strongest spirit atop a ecosystem who has to work to retain dominance as city's evolve and change.<br /> <br /> For Example -<br /> <br /> The Spirit of San Francisco, born from roots of being a Missionary outpost, has evolved from rough and tumble frontier town, to be a gateway to the far east, to a military town, to the center of the Counter Culture, to a bastion of LGBTQ rights, to its current evolving role as a capital of technological industry. You could present each of these incarnations as separate spirits, or perhaps a long,strange evolution of a single powerful spirit.<br /> <br /> The Spirit of Los Angeles might be a spirit born from migrants and missionaries; growing into a spirit of power and opportunity, but has to share its rule with Hollywood, a spirit of fame and glamour, grown strong on a million dreams.<br /> <br /> New York may not be one spirit but five, with each borough (Manhattan, the Bronx, Queens, Brooklyn, and Staten Island) having its own power,character, and realm of influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T12:42:51-07:00","id":1196878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196803-spirits-of-cities?p=1196860#post1196860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if it helps, here's how I think of it:<br /> Spirits start out as reflections of a discrete thing; they grow in rank as that thing gains prominance and they branch out to general categories and multiple influences (by consuming more essence - implying intensive competition, even the consumption of their rivals).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also how I think about it. In my Spain setting, the current soirit of Spain was originally a Spirit of the Reconquista, combining both military and catholic faith elements. During Reconquista, it grow consuming other similar spirits and Islam-linked spirits (as its natursl prey). At the end, with the support of a wewrewolf lodge (the Crusaders of Santiago), it became the most powerful dpirit in Spain.<br /> <br /> There's other pretendants to the tittle, as Lady Republic, a mad magath (originally an spirit of liberalism and revolution) who combines aspects of revolutionary ideologies (as classical liberalism, socialism, communism, anarchism).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T12:53:20-07:00","id":1196882,"title":"","content":"FYI, this discussion informed this story seed idea: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks?p=1196881#post1196881\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...81#post1196881</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T13:11:07-07:00","id":1196887,"title":"","content":"Cities like St. Louis and Detroit have spirits that used to be powerful, but have become starved of Essence as the cities themselves decline. I imagine the Spirit of St. Louis (heh) used to have Influences over Exploration and Innovation, and now it's just fighting a holding action against all the upstart suburban spirits that surround it....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T13:34:47-07:00","id":1196893,"title":"","content":"Since I live near can you do the twin cities","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T14:48:32-07:00","id":1196909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196803-spirits-of-cities?p=1196893#post1196893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I live near can you do the twin cities</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a perfect place for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190223-forsaken-february-heralds-of-the-firstborn?p=1194919#post1194919\">Twin Beings</a> Numen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T15:36:00-07:00","id":1197357,"title":"","content":"I would like to try and design a few spirits of great cities, but since they are probably at least Rank 6 there are no rules to support them. I suppose I could extrapolate how much of every stat a Rank 6+ entity would have but I'm not going to invest my time in it. It would maybe serve me better to simply treat them as plot elements, impossible to affect or confront by even the most powerful of player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T16:16:19-07:00","id":1197380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196803-spirits-of-cities?p=1197357#post1197357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to try and design a few spirits of great cities, but since they are probably at least Rank 6 there are no rules to support them. I suppose I could extrapolate how much of every stat a Rank 6+ entity would have but I'm not going to invest my time in it. It would maybe serve me better to simply treat them as plot elements, impossible to affect or confront by even the most powerful of player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are always Royal Avatars to use. Identify which god-like facet you want to embody, and run with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T16:55:26-07:00","id":1197392,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Rank 6+ beings usually split off 'Royal Avatars' of themselves, Rank 5 entities that personify a facet of the higher entity's being.<br /> <br /> Here's a couple for Forsaken's Firstborn. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190223-forsaken-february-heralds-of-the-firstborn?p=1192771#post1192771\">The Knight of the Crossroads</a>. And <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190223-forsaken-february-heralds-of-the-firstborn?p=1194919#post1194919\">Artifice &amp; Industry</a>. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190223-forsaken-february-heralds-of-the-firstborn?p=1193680#post1193680\">The Monarch Wreathed in Calamity</a> is in there too but without a write-up. The Summoners book has one, the Thunderer.<br /> <br /> Acrozatarim wrote up some example <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171004-ten-spirits-binded?p=1172094#post1172094\">Spirit Noble Numina</a>, too, that might be useful in depicting this sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T22:55:23-07:00","id":1197494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196803-spirits-of-cities?p=1197392#post1197392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Rank 6+ beings usually split off 'Royal Avatars' of themselves, Rank 5 entities that personify a facet of the higher entity's being.<br /> <br /> Here's a couple for Forsaken's Firstborn. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190223-forsaken-february-heralds-of-the-firstborn?p=1192771#post1192771\">The Knight of the Crossroads</a>. And <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190223-forsaken-february-heralds-of-the-firstborn?p=1194919#post1194919\">Artifice &amp; Industry</a>. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190223-forsaken-february-heralds-of-the-firstborn?p=1193680#post1193680\">The Monarch Wreathed in Calamity</a> is in there too but without a write-up. The Summoners book has one, the Thunderer.<br /> <br /> Acrozatarim wrote up some example <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171004-ten-spirits-binded?p=1172094#post1172094\">Spirit Noble Numina</a>, too, that might be useful in depicting this sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are excellent links, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}